{
  "summary": "Transaction lookup routines in node::GetTransaction and TxIndex::FindTx/FindLegacyTx are updated to throw std::runtime_error on disk I/O, deserialization, and index corruption failures rather than returning null. ProcessPSBT is refactored to reuse GetTransaction instead of doing duplicate lookups. Additionally, getrawtransaction with an explicit block hash now invokes CheckBlockDataAvailability to distinguish pruned or not-yet-downloaded blocks from missing transactions.",
  "problem": "When disk reads or index lookups fail due to file I/O or corrupt index entries, transaction retrieval returns null or nullopt, which callers interpret as a non-existent transaction. As a result, confirmed transactions appear missing and underlying disk failures or index corruptions go undetected by RPC clients and node operators.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit e0b20465bb: 'Currently the GetTransaction return value is a nullable transaction pointer, where nullptr represents two different outcomes: I/O error and missing tx. Reporting a confirmed transaction as missing is wrong, so properly return an error instead.'",
    "Commit e0b20465bb: '...a -txindex corruption may also point to a larger system corruption and it seems better to notify the user properly by throwing an exception.'"
  ],
